From 923f7340a0b21e882082304d8a1f6e0aa43fbc75 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 31 Jul 2026 09:26:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v1.9.9: Wireless Diagnostics robustness - PID-aware
 scan/capture token reclaim, band-generic pin dialog, quad-band labels

Field feedback (Wireless > Wireless Diagnostics): Apply Best Channel / Auto Scan
misbehaving - unresponsive buttons, "error" on scan, silent capture failure,
"applies to 6 GHz regardless of band". Root causes and fixes:

- #1 PID-aware token reclaim (web.c): a stale /tmp/reaper_wifi/{run,scanrun} left
  by a worker killed mid-sweep (e.g. a wireless restart) wedged BOTH scan and
  capture for 400/600s, and the status handler's bare-existence check disabled the
  Start buttons + forced poll mode ("buttons not responding"). New rwifi_token_live()
  judges a job by worker-PID liveness (kill(pid,0)); workers stamp their own PID,
  the parent writes a "0" placeholder.
- #6 capture worker unlinks its token on both early-exit paths (was stranding it -
  a concrete instance of #1; the scan worker already cleaned up).
- #3/#4 capStart() parses the CGI response and surfaces errors via a toast instead
  of silently polling nothing; scan-busy is attributed correctly (busycap = a
  capture is running, busy = another scan).
- #5 band-generic strings: RWIF_42 "Pin 6 GHz to this channel?" -> "Pin the best
  channel to this radio?" with the real band injected; RWIF_37/38 drop the "6 GHz"
  hardcode. This mislabel is the likely origin of the "targets 6 GHz" report - the
  dialog said 6 GHz on every band.
- #2 own-band abort: scanning the band your browser is on drops you each restart ->
  heartbeat lapses -> abort+restore = "no change". New RWIF_60 explains it; a
  user-stop flag distinguishes it from RWIF_39.
- #7 quad-band: bandLabel() disambiguates the two "5 GHz" selector entries.

i18n: new RWIF_59/60 + reworded RWIF_37/38/42 across all 25 dicts in lockstep
(machine-translated non-EN - native/langcheck review pending). Metal-only
validatable (the mock cannot render this page).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
